TEXT -264 528 Left 2 ;pickup coil\n320 ohm / 66 mH\ncold end sits on\nthe bias node
TEXT 40 616 Left 2 ;matched dual N-JFET, one package.\nThe loop forces V(D1)=V(D2), hence\nId1=Id2, hence Vg1=Vg2: the operating\npoint is set by the loop, not by Idss.
TEXT 1144 104 Left 2 ;lead-lag across the\ndrains. Differential\nonly - does not touch\nthe common mode.
TEXT 1504 648 Left 2 ;same 15k / 2k2 / 22u shelf\nas the OPA376 stage:\ngain 7.8, zero 0.42 Hz,\npole 3.29 Hz, unity at DC
TEXT 1560 240 Left 2 ;converter input\n+ cable
TEXT 1920 512 Left 2 ;1.0 V bias reference,\nshared by four channels
TEXT 112 880 Left 2 !.inc jfet_composite.lib\n.param Vrail=3.3\n; grade corner set in the .lib\n.param Rin=1k  Cin=100p\n.param Rd=5.6k Rt=4.75k\n.param Rcz=4.7k Ccz=390p\n.param Rf=15k  Rg=2.2k Cg=22u\n.param Lcoil=66m Rcoil=320 Ccoil=1f
TEXT 616 896 Left 2 !;.op\n;.ac dec 40 0.1 10meg\n;.noise V(OUT) Vsig dec 20 10 20k\n.tran 0 120m 60m\n;; corners: swap K2145T -> K2145L / K2145H on both JFETs
TEXT 1360 952 Left 2 ;Uncomment one analysis at a time.\n.op       - bias point; V(OUT) should land on the bias reference\n.ac       - 17.8 dB midband, -3 dB at 3.2 Hz, -17.9 dB shelf below\n.noise    - input-referred noise at V(OUT)\n.step     - walks the JFET grade corners; V(OUT) should not move
TEXT 112 1080 Left 2 ;Dual-JFET / opamp composite string front end - single 3.3 V analog rail.\nThe JFET pair replaces the opamp's own input stage: the opamp's noise and offset are\nreferred back divided by the pair's stage gain (about 14x here), which is what lets a\n30 nV/rtHz, 60 uA amplifier sit where a 7.5 nV/rtHz, 760 uA one used to.
